{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.PNeqNpWallUnification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.PNeqNpWallUnification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinGradeConnective","lean:module:QOU.Information.CountingModuliGrade"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_physicalCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_physicalCost","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpWallUnification.lean#L50-L66","doc":"**The moduli `physicalCost` drives the same bridge separation (sorry-free).**\nThe `3^{3n}` resolution-tree cost of `CountingModuliGrade` is another instance\nof the general super-poly-cost lemma (via `physicalCost_superPoly`).  So the\nsame super-polynomial cost witness that powers the moduli\n`FamilyPolyBounded` separation (`not_familyPolyBounded_of_physical_point`)\nalso powers this bridge `PolyObservable` separation — the two walls consume\none shared ingredient (`physicalCost_superPoly`), though the predicates\n(`FamilyPolyBounded` vs `PolyObservable`) are distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physicalCost_eq_three_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physicalCost_eq_three_pow","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpWallUnification.lean#L46-L48","doc":"`physicalCost n = 3^{3n}` — the moduli counting cost is a bridge horizon cost\nat filtration level `3n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}